  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.58,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "extra_component",
      "components": ["J3"],
      "pins": ["J3.1", "J3.2"],
      "nets": ["GND", "/Microcontroller/NET0004"],
      "observed": "A 2-pin screw terminal J3 is present in the Microcontroller sheet with pin 1 tied to GND and pin 2 tied to the heater-control net /Microcontroller/NET0004, which also carries ESP32 GPIO1 and the TPS1H200 IN/DIAG_EN pins.",
      "expected": "The specification describes screw terminals only for thermocouple inputs and the heater output; it does not describe a user-accessible screw terminal tied to the GPIO1/IN/DIAG_EN control net. A control signal should not be broken out to a shortable screw terminal without a documented purpose or protection.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "net (code \"5\") (name \"/Microcontroller/NET0004\") ... (node (ref \"J3\") (pin \"2\")) ... (node (ref \"U8\") (pin \"13\") (pinfunction \"GPIO1...\")) ... (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"IN\")) ... (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"DIAG_EN\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "net (code \"8\") (name \"GND\") ... (node (ref \"J3\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"Pin_1\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "IN/DIAG_EN (pins 1/2) are both driven from ESP32 GPIO1 (net /Microcontroller/HEATER), OUT (pin 7) feeds the heater connector J6 pin 2"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If a wire or jumper is connected across J3, GPIO1 and the heater-switch control input are shorted to ground, preventing heater enable and loading the MCU. If the terminal is mistaken for a thermocouple or heater terminal, it can cause incorrect sensing or heater control.",
      "confidence": 0.58
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Most power, SPI, thermocouple, heater-switch, fan, and USB connections match the intended design despite reference renumbering. The main suspicious deviation is the extra screw terminal J3 tied between GND and the GPIO1/IN/DIAG_EN heater-control net, which is not described in the specification and creates a user-accessible short-to-ground on a control signal."
}

